## Embedded Containers & Data
<hr class="section-rule lvl-2">

!!! warning "<small>Mad Science</small>"
    Reasonable people might consider this to be mad science.  See [this section]({{_}}/matrioshka/#has-science-gone-too-far) for more discussion on that point, and if you're more interested in patterns and theory, then you might prefer to start [here]({{_}}/matrioshka).

Sometimes it's useful to declare **inlined containers and data**[^compose] alongside the same automation that is making use of those containers.  You'll have to exercise some judgement about when and where that is a *good idea*, but since tool containers tend to be small and change infrequently, **being self-contained reduces change-related friction and context-switching** that's associated with external repositories, external registries, and external files.

